#: ../../../envvar/CTEST_DISABLE_INSTRUMENTATION.rst:2
msgid "CTEST_DISABLE_INSTRUMENTATION"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/include/ENV_VAR.rst:1
msgid ""
"This is a CMake :ref:`Environment Variable <CMake Language Environment "
"Variables>`. Its initial value is taken from the calling process environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CTEST_DISABLE_INSTRUMENTATION.rst:8
msgid ""
"When set to a true value, such as ``1``, ``True``, or ``ON``, this "
"environment variable disables all :manual:`CMake instrumentation <cmake-"
"instrumentation(7)>` data collection, indexing hooks, and callbacks. This "
"includes manual indexing with :option:`ctest --collect-instrumentation`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CTEST_DISABLE_INSTRUMENTATION.rst:13
msgid ""
"This setting takes precedence over project-level and user-level queries, "
"the :command:`cmake_instrumentation` command, and "
"the :envvar:`CTEST_USE_INSTRUMENTATION` "
"and :envvar:`CTEST_USE_VERBOSE_INSTRUMENTATION` environment variables. It "
"also applies when building or testing an already-configured build tree. "
"Queries are still loaded and generated normally, but no instrumentation data "
"is collected or indexed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CTEST_DISABLE_INSTRUMENTATION.rst:21
msgid ""
"Unset the variable, or set it to a false value such as ``0``, ``OFF``, or an "
"empty string, to allow instrumentation to operate normally."
msgstr ""
